From: kevin03L <kevin03L@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] workqueue: do not leave a pwq pending without work after a thaw

After some suspends of a Jetson Nano the GPU stayed at whatever frequency it had, at full load too:
devfreq's monitor never ran again. Its work item was inactive on a workqueue with nothing active:

  workqueue devfreq_wq: flags=0x4000e
    pwq 16: cpus=0-3 flags=0x4 nice=0 active=0 refcnt=2
      inactive: devfreq_monitor

devfreq_wq is unbound and freezable, with max_active 1. While it is frozen max_active is 0, so the
monitor's work item, queued by its timer, becomes inactive and its pwq goes on the node's
pending_pwqs. devfreq_suspend() then cancels the item, but the pwq stays on the list. That is
normally harmless: the next pwq_dec_nr_active() drops a pwq without inactive work. Here nothing is
active, so nothing calls it; pwq_tryinc_nr_active() sees the pwq pending and refuses, for ever, to
activate the next item.

When max_active goes up again, drop such a pwq from pending_pwqs. It is done under the pool lock
together with the attempt to activate, so an item queued later finds a clean pwq.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/kernel/workqueue.c
+++ b/kernel/workqueue.c
@@ -5735,6 +5735,29 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * Take @pwq off its node's pending_pwqs when it has no inactive work item left.
+ *
+ * While a freezable workqueue is frozen its max_active is zero: a queued work
+ * item becomes inactive and its pwq pending. If the item is cancelled before
+ * the thaw, the pwq stays pending with nothing to activate, and as nothing is
+ * active either, no pwq_dec_nr_active() comes to clean it up. The next work
+ * item would see the pwq pending, take its place behind it and never run.
+ */
+static void pwq_drop_stale_pending(struct pool_workqueue *pwq)
+{
+	struct wq_node_nr_active *nna = wq_node_nr_active(pwq->wq, pwq->pool->node);
+
+	lockdep_assert_held(&pwq->pool->lock);
+
+	if (!nna || !list_empty(&pwq->inactive_works))
+		return;
+
+	raw_spin_lock(&nna->lock);
+	list_del_init(&pwq->pending_node);
+	raw_spin_unlock(&nna->lock);
+}
+
 /**
  * wq_adjust_max_active - update a wq's max_active to the current setting
  * @wq: target workqueue
@@ -5792,6 +5815,8 @@
 			if (pwq_activate_first_inactive(pwq, true)) {
 				activated = true;
 				kick_pool(pwq->pool);
+			} else {
+				pwq_drop_stale_pending(pwq);
 			}
 			raw_spin_unlock_irqrestore(&pwq->pool->lock, irq_flags);
 		}
